<h2 id="ha-ctrl-001-acceptance">Acceptance and evidence</h2>

1. Use fixtures for a valid 0, a negative reading, `unknown`, `unavailable`, an assumed state, an absent attribute and an explicit `null`. Compare the visible text and the accessible name.
2. Hold a value constant while reports keep arriving, then stop the reports under a documented rhythm. Only the second case may become stale. Include an integration that does not rewrite unchanged states.
3. Remove and restore the entity while a details view is open. Keep the name and focus, and do not show an older value as current.
4. Check long names, the native locale, the repeated hour when the clocks go back, dark mode and forced colours.

Record the Home Assistant and frontend versions, browser, fixture or device, input state, expected result, observed result and where the evidence is kept. Reviewing the source or this page is not a test on a connected device.

For the native definitions, see the Home Assistant documentation for the [state and state object](https://www.home-assistant.io/docs/configuration/state_object/).
